The open sets of a metric space satisfy the axioms, by [[Open Sets in Metric Space form Topology]].
The converse fails without further hypotheses: a non-[[Definition:Hausdorff Space|Hausdorff]] topology is not [[Definition:Metrizable Topology|metrizable]], and metrizability requires conditions as in [[Urysohn's Metrization Theorem]].
